Large activations in the inspected data concentrate at row/document starts.
Most word-like openings get a negative pulse; numbers and whitespace do not.
Comments, headings, code-opening words and the definite article refine its size.
The pulse survives repetitions of the identical opening token, then stops.
Individual-token amplitude differences beyond these classes are not modeled.
